:: Woods Abandoned Campsite [nobr]

/* Written by: Winters */
/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>

The sun filters through the thick canopy overhead, causing golden spots to dance across your body. Maneuvering around trees that loom over you like towering sentinels, and thick brambles of bushes, you meander through the forest. The branches rustling overhead, the low-level hum of buzzling insects, and the rustle of hidden animals create a medley of sounds that fills your ears. Branches claw at you from the low hanging canopy, as you weave through the maze of underbrush. The air is thick with the damp, heavy scent of rotting leaves. <br>
<br>
However, a moment later, the forest abruptly stops as you step into an unexpected clearing. Compared to the dim forest, the unobstructed sunlight in this clearing is so bright that you squint slightly. Compared to the forest, there is an eerie, pristine silence to the clearing. As your eyes adjust to the light change, what almost immediately catches your attention is the abandoned campsite in the center of the clearing. <span style="color:Yellow">At least, you think it’s abandoned.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

You find yourself moving closer to the campsite. At the center of the campsite is a ring of soot-stained rocks surrounding a bed of charcoal and ashes. Poking out of the ash is a crushed aluminum soda can. Nudging it with your foot, it emits a thin, tinny scrape against the rocks. A small puddle of stagnant rainwater sloshes out of the mouth of the can. <br>
<br>
Looking past the fire pit is the skeletal remains of a tent, that is nearly fully collapsed. The fabric has several large tears in it, along with large patches of decay. You approach carefully, using a sturdy stick to peel back a flap of the moldering door. <br>
<br>
Inside, it is mostly trash covering an old foam sleeping pad. <span style="color:Yellow">Then, tucked amongst the wreckage of the tent, you spot it.</span> <br>
<br>

<<set _random to random(1, 3)>>

<<if _random == 1>>
    It’s an old, brown glass beer bottle. The label has peeled away, leaving only a sticky, gray residue where the glue used to be. You pick it up by the neck. It’s surprisingly heavy. Holding it up to the sunlight, you see that there is still liquid inside. Someone put the twist cap back on, preserving the remnants inside the bottle. As you look at the liquid gently sloshing about, a thought pops into your head, both unbidden and intrusive. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:Yellow">What does beer taste like?</span> <br>
    <br>
    <div id="choice">
        <<link "Leave it alone<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            This thought lingers in your mind for a moment, before you shake your head. The beer must have been open for quite a while, and it likely has gone bad as a result. Better not try and potentially get sick from it. <br>
            <br>
            Besides, it’s fun being a kid and not having to deal with adult stuff. Setting the bottle down, you stand back up, brushing your hands as you do so. A sudden, sharp gust of wind causes a piece of the wrecked tent to flap violently. You take a step back, looking over the forgotten camp one last time. <br>
            <br>
            Turning on your heel, you head back toward the edge of the woods, the sound of your footsteps once again joining the melody of noises as the forest closes in around you. <br>
