            <br>
            You go to twist off the rusted cap. It gives way after an exerted effort. There is no hiss of carbonation, which you’re pretty sure should happen with beer. Instead, it is just a dull scape of the rusted cap against the glass. <br>
            <br>
            You bring the rim to your nose. It smells sweet, metallic, and deeply sour, like rotting fruit left out in the sun. You hesitate. Your stomach tightens in warning. But you tilt the bottle anyway, resolving just to take a small sip. Just enough to say that you did. <br>
            <br>
