            <span style="color:LightCoral">You retch, coughing violently as your stomach turns inside out. You spit frantically, trying to scrub the horrific taste off your tongue with the back of your arm, your eyes watering so badly the trees blur into a smear of green and brown. For a terrifying minute, you're convinced you've poisoned yourself. You wipe your mouth, gasping for the clean forest air, your chest heaving.</span> <br>
            <br>
            Slowly, the nausea subsides, leaving only a burning throat and a profound sense of foolishness. You stand up on shaky legs, wiping a tear from your cheek. The forest doesn’t feel like a grand adventure anymore. They just feel cold. Turning on your heel, you break into a jog, eager to leave the old campsite, and memories of that awful taste, far behind. <br>
