            You pull your hands back, shaking them clean with a grimace. <span style="color:LightCoral">Your fingers smell like mildew and stagnant swamp water.</span> You wipe them off on the grass, looking down at the ruined pile of paper. The mystery is gone, replaced only by a mess of wet pulp and dirt. <br>
