    On the ground is what looks like a cylindrical piece of translucent deflated rubber. After staring at it for a few seconds, you suspect you know what it is. You've heard the older kids at school talk about these things in hushed, giggling whispers, but you’ve never actually seen one in real life. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:Pink">It’s a used condom.</span> <br>
    <br>
    Exposure to the elements have turned the latex a milky, opaque yellowish-gray. It looks ancient, shriveled at the end, and caked with a thin layer of grit and dried forest grime. You continue to stare at it for a long moment, your heart hammering against your ribs as you look at something so taboo. <br>
    <br> 
    An intrusive, utterly bizarre thought pops into your head. A mix of profound curiosity and the dumb, reckless daredevil energy that only strikes when you are entirely alone in the woods. <span style="color:Yellow">You wonder how it works and feels. <br>
    <br>
    Almost without thinking, you reach out towards it.</span> <br>
    <br>
